exit=0
--- stdout ---
Create or replace a JWT auth profile: a named issuer configuration for
bearer-token admission that LB rules reference by name (POST
/config/ai/jwtauthprofile). Posting an existing name replaces the profile
and restarts its key lifecycle: the profile answers 503-class on the data
plane until the first JWKS fetch against the new configuration succeeds.
Only public key material is ever fetched or held. A successful create is
not proof the issuer is reachable; activation does not wait for the fetch.

Claim extraction is dot-paths because the identity provider owns the
claim schema; the defaults are Keycloak-shaped. A numeric flag left at
zero selects the gateway's documented default. What the gateway refuses
(an issuer that is not an http(s) URL, an algorithm it never accepts) is
printed as it answers.

ex)
	loxicmd create jwtauthprofile keycloak --issuer=https://sso.example.com/realms/ai
	loxicmd create jwtauthprofile okta --issuer=https://example.okta.com --audiences=ai-gateway --tenant-claim=org_id --priority-class=critical

Usage:
  loxicmd create jwtauthprofile <NAME> --issuer=<url> [--jwks-url=<url>] [--audiences=<aud>,] [--algs=<alg>,] [--leeway-sec=<n>] [--refresh-sec=<n>] [--tenant-claim=<path>] [--user-claim=<path>] [--models-claim=<path>] [--roles-claim=<path>] [--model-role-prefix=<prefix>] [--username-claim=<path>] [--model-authz=claims-required|allow-all] [--default-tenant=<tenant>] [--forward-identity] [--authorization-passthrough] [--priority-class=<class>] [flags]

Aliases:
  jwtauthprofile, jwtauthprofiles, jwtprofile

Flags:
      --algs strings                Signature-algorithm accept-list (RS256/RS384/RS512, ES256/ES384/ES512, PS256/PS384/PS512); default RS256,ES256. alg=none and HMAC are refused by the gateway unconditionally
      --audiences strings           Accept-list matched against the token aud values and azp; at least one must match. Empty skips the audience check
      --authorization-passthrough   Leave the client Authorization header on the upstream request instead of stripping it after verification
      --default-tenant string       Tenant used when the tenant claim is absent. Empty means such tokens are denied (401): an unattributable request cannot be metered
      --forward-identity            Inject verified X-Auth-Tenant/X-Auth-User headers upstream (client-sent copies are always stripped)
  -h, --help                        help for jwtauthprofile
      --issuer string               Exact string the token iss claim must equal; an http(s) URL. When --jwks-url is unset it is also the base for OIDC discovery (issuer + /.well-known/openid-configuration) (required)
      --jwks-url string             Overrides OIDC discovery of the JWKS endpoint when set
      --leeway-sec int              Clock-skew allowance in seconds for exp/nbf/iat (gateway default 30)
      --model-authz string          What happens when no model list can be derived from the token: claims-required (default) denies every model; allow-all admits any model for an otherwise-valid token
      --model-role-prefix string    Prefix filter turning roles into allowed models (gateway default "model:")
      --models-claim string         Dot-path to a string array of allowed models. Unset derives models from roles via --model-role-prefix; when set and present in the token it is authoritative, even when empty
      --priority-class string       The highest priority class a request admitted by this profile's tokens may have: standard, critical or sheddable. It can only lower what the tenant allows; omitted means no cap from the profile
      --refresh-sec int             Periodic JWKS refresh interval in seconds (gateway default 3600)
      --roles-claim string          Dot-path to the roles array (gateway default realm_access.roles)
      --tenant-claim string         Dot-path to the tenant identity claim (gateway default tenant_id)
      --user-claim string           Dot-path to the stable user identity claim (gateway default sub)
      --username-claim string       Dot-path to a display-only username (gateway default preferred_username)

Global Flags:
  -s, --apiserver string    Set API server IP address (default "127.0.0.1")
      --bearer              Send the token as 'Authorization: Bearer <token>' (required by the inference gateway; disable for classic loxilb raw-token targets) (default true)
      --cacert string       CA certificate (PEM) to verify the server (https only)
      --cert string         Client certificate (PEM) for mutual TLS (https only)
  -k, --insecure            Skip TLS certificate verification (https only)
      --key string          Client private key (PEM) for mutual TLS (https only)
      --originator          Name this invocation in the gateway's audit trail as 'cli:<os user>@<host>', sent as the X-Loxilb-Originator header (for a service account driving the CLI)
  -o, --output string       Set output layer (ex.) wide, json)
  -p, --port int            Set API server port number (default 11111)
      --protocol string     Set API server http/https (default "http")
  -t, --timeout int16       Set timeout (default 10)
      --token string        Set Token for the API server (deprecated: the value is visible in shell history and process listings; use --token-file)
      --token-file string   Read the API server token from an owner-only (0600) regular file; replaces the deprecated --token
